1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,220
My name's Biscuit Kruger, and I'm a professional hunter.

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:11,400
But I'm not too big on formalities, so you guys can just call me Biscuit.

3
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:16,140
In return, you must obey every word of what I teach you without question.

4
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:18,440
Ugh, no way and no thank you.

5
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:24,180
He and I are not so desperate that we need to beg a total stranger to train us so you can just forget about it.

6
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,120
Am I right, Gon? Back me up!

7
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,960
The thing is, Mr. Wing is already training us.

8
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:35,100
Yeah, that's right. We already have a master, positions filled, and we are not in the market for another one.

9
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,820
Did you say Wing? That little boy with the messy hair and glasses?

10
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:42,080
The one who never tucks his shirt in?

11
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,280
You know him?

12
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:47,880
Well, of course I know him. Wing is one of my students. Or he was.

13
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,140
Really? Wow, what a coincidence, huh?

14
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:56,020
So Wing's become a master now, has he? Time really does fly, doesn't it?

15
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:59,140
Does that mean both of you are professional hunters as well?

16
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,180
Yeah, well, just me.

17
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,900
And you've passed the secret exam too?

18
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:04,600
Yep.

19
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,380
Wow, that really takes me back.

20
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:10,420
I'd love to be an examiner again.

21
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:16,220
Well, I guess that would mean that I am essentially your master's master.

22
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:19,080
Know that that's out of the way. Let's start training!

23
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:49,060
Let's start training!

24
00:01:49,080 --> 00:02:19,060
Let's start training!

25
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:49,060
Let's start training!

26
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:57,520
That is so awesome!

27
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:00,200
You were really one of the examiners for the hunter exam?

28
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,740
Well, I'm not convinced that she's telling the truth.

29
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:06,140
You sure are a stubborn little boy, aren't you?

30
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,340
That's a good thing.

31
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,280
And kids, anyway.

32
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:12,080
Now, you mentioned before that you weren't desperate, right?

33
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:13,420
Look!

34
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,620
What's that card?

35
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:18,740
Notice that the difficulty to obtain is rank D.

36
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:22,360
It's a normal card that doesn't go in a specified slot in your book.

37
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:28,080
There are a lot of people who could have obtained this card without much trouble.

38
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,120
The same can't be said for you two.

39
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,360
And that's the problem.

40
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:35,180
If you run into someone who's stronger than you are,

41
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:38,080
or someone whose intentions are completely evil...

42
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,320
Quick, sit down.

43
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,700
Pretend we're just chatting.

44
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,960
There's an enemy behind me.

45
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:51,480
Three kids will be a walk in the park.

46
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:58,460
